{"id": "2026-10-08-news-russian-strike-kills-30-in-kramatorsk", "date": "2026-10-08", "stream": "news", "headline": "Russian strike kills 30 in Kramatorsk", "summary": "A Russian strike on Kramatorsk on the morning of Thursday 8 October killed at least 30 people and injured 18, Ukrainian officials said.", "url": "https://kyivindependent.com/at-least-12-dead-after-russian-glide-bomb-strikes-kramatorsk-bus-stop/", "source_domain": "kyivindependent.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "A Russian strike on Kramatorsk on the morning of Thursday 8 October killed at least 30 people and injured 18, Ukrainian officials said. Donetsk regional governor Vadym Filashkin said a glide bomb (a heavy bomb fitted with wings and guidance, released from aircraft well behind the front line) hit a bus stop, and photos he shared show at least one burned-out bus. Kramatorsk mayor Oleksandr Hontcharenko, quoted by Le Monde, said two scheduled buses were hit. The Kramatorsk and Sloviansk military administrations suspended all public transport. Overnight, Russia also launched 142 Shahed-type drones across Ukraine, of which the air force said 126 were shot down or suppressed.", "why": "the strike came one day after Russia's mass missile and drone attack on Ukrainian cities, and it targeted civilian transport in a front-line region where civilians are still being evacuated.", "thread_id": "2026-10-08-news-russian-strike-kills-30-in-kramatorsk", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-08", "event_date": "2026-10-08", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Russia", "Ukraine", "Kramatorsk"]}
{"id": "2026-10-08-news-uk-keeps-east-jerusalem-post-as-a-mission", "date": "2026-10-08", "stream": "news", "headline": "UK keeps East Jerusalem post as a mission", "summary": "Britain said on Thursday 8 October that its consulate-general in East Jerusalem will stay open as a \"UK mission\", with only seven diplomats remaining, after Israel ordered the consulate to close that day.", "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/oct/08/uk-consulate-east-jerusalem-remain-open-uk-mission-ed-miliband", "source_domain": "theguardian.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Britain said on Thursday 8 October that its consulate-general in East Jerusalem will stay open as a \"UK mission\", with only seven diplomats remaining, after Israel ordered the consulate to close that day. Israel's foreign minister Gideon Sa'ar presented the move as punishment for Foreign Secretary Ed Miliband's decision last month to ban trade with Israeli settlements, which Britain considers illegal, and to tighten sanctions on people who help build them. Sa'ar also announced entry bans for 12 named people, including former Labour leader Jeremy Corbyn. Miliband dropped a plan to expel Israeli diplomats from London and said there would be no reciprocal measures while talks continue, but restated that \"East Jerusalem is occupied territory\". The consulate, which serves Palestinians in East Jerusalem, the West Bank and Gaza, loses about 20 staff.", "why": "Western diplomats had feared that a full closure would set a precedent for other countries' missions to the Palestinians, ahead of Israel's election on Tuesday 27 October.", "thread_id": "2026-10-08-news-uk-keeps-east-jerusalem-post-as-a-mission", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-08", "event_date": "2026-10-08", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["United Kingdom", "Israel", "East Jerusalem", "Ed Miliband"]}
{"id": "2026-10-08-news-houthis-claim-deadly-hit-on-riyadh-airport", "date": "2026-10-08", "stream": "news", "headline": "Houthis claim deadly hit on Riyadh airport", "summary": "Yemen's Houthis said on Thursday 8 October that a ballistic missile hit King Khalid International Airport in Riyadh, killing three people, while the Saudi-led coalition said it had destroyed 82 Houthi military targets.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/yemen-s-houthis-claim-strike-on-riyadh-airport-three-killed/a-79587815", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Yemen's Houthis said on Thursday 8 October that a ballistic missile hit King Khalid International Airport in Riyadh, killing three people, while the Saudi-led coalition said it had destroyed 82 Houthi military targets. It is the third time this week the Houthis have claimed an attack on the airport. Their spokesman, Yahya Saree, also warned international airlines \"for the last time\" to stop flying through Saudi airspace. Coalition spokesman Turki al-Maliki said the strikes hit targets in Saada, Marib, Al Jawf and Al Hudaydah provinces, without giving details of casualties. Neither side's claims could be independently verified, and Saudi Arabia had not confirmed any deaths at the airport. The day before, Yemen's internationally recognised government announced a major counteroffensive.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-08-news-houthis-claim-deadly-hit-on-riyadh-airport", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-08", "event_date": "2026-10-08", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Houthis", "Saudi Arabia", "Yemen", "Riyadh"]}
{"id": "2026-10-08-news-tanker-hit-by-projectiles-off-qatar", "date": "2026-10-08", "stream": "news", "headline": "Tanker hit by projectiles off Qatar", "summary": "A tanker was hit by several projectiles 94 kilometres north of Madinat ash Shamal, off Qatar's northern coast, on Wednesday 7 October, and casualties were reported, the UK Maritime Trade Operations agency (UKMTO, a British navy-run shipping security service) said.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/8/tanker-hit-by-multiple-projectiles-off-north-coast-of-qatar-ukmto-says", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "A tanker was hit by several projectiles 94 kilometres north of Madinat ash Shamal, off Qatar's northern coast, on Wednesday 7 October, and casualties were reported, the UK Maritime Trade Operations agency (UKMTO, a British navy-run shipping security service) said. UKMTO did not say how many people were killed or injured, or where the ship came from. Qatar has not commented, although the attack happened inside its exclusive economic zone. Attacks this far west in the Gulf are unusual. Most have been in the Strait of Hormuz, where UKMTO counted nine attacks on tankers in October so far. Iran has effectively closed the strait since the US-Israeli war on Iran began on 28 February.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-08-news-tanker-hit-by-projectiles-off-qatar", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-08", "event_date": "2026-10-07", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["UKMTO", "Qatar", "Strait of Hormuz"]}
{"id": "2026-10-08-news-south-korea-recalls-its-envoy-to-ukraine", "date": "2026-10-08", "stream": "news", "headline": "South Korea recalls its envoy to Ukraine", "summary": "South Korea said on Thursday 8 October that it is recalling its ambassador to Ukraine, Park Hee-chang, in a dispute over two North Korean prisoners of war that Ukraine transferred to South Korea.", "url": "https://kyivindependent.com/south-korea-to-recall-ukraine-envoy-amid-north-korean-pows-dispute/", "source_domain": "kyivindependent.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "South Korea said on Thursday 8 October that it is recalling its ambassador to Ukraine, Park Hee-chang, in a dispute over two North Korean prisoners of war that Ukraine transferred to South Korea. Seoul says President Volodymyr Zelensky broke a confidentiality agreement when he announced the transfer in his UN speech on 23 September. Zelensky's office says no such agreement existed. South Korea's foreign minister, Cho Hyun, said on 6 October that the regret expressed by his Ukrainian counterpart Andrii Sybiha was not \"the level we expect\". Separately, Seoul has threatened legal action if fuel shipments to Russia are found to have broken South Korean law.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-08-news-south-korea-recalls-its-envoy-to-ukraine", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-08", "event_date": "2026-10-08", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["South Korea", "Ukraine", "North Korea"]}
{"id": "2026-10-08-news-imf-strikes-1-21bn-staff-deal-with-pakistan", "date": "2026-10-08", "stream": "news", "headline": "IMF strikes $1.21bn staff deal with Pakistan", "summary": "The International Monetary Fund said on Wednesday 7 October it had reached a staff-level agreement with Pakistan that could release about $1.21 billion.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/imf-reaches-tentative-1-21-billion-bailout-deal-with-pakistan/a-79587047", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["economy", "world"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "The International Monetary Fund said on Wednesday 7 October it had reached a staff-level agreement with Pakistan that could release about $1.21 billion. A staff-level agreement is a deal between IMF negotiators and the government; the Fund's Executive Board must still approve it before any money is paid. IMF negotiator Iva Petrova said growth had slowed because of \"higher energy prices and supply disruptions\" linked to the Middle East war. Growth for the full fiscal year is estimated at 3.6%, and inflation eased to about 10.3% in September after peaking in May.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-08-news-imf-strikes-1-21bn-staff-deal-with-pakistan", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-08", "event_date": "2026-10-07", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["IMF", "Pakistan"]}
{"id": "2026-10-08-news-china-nominates-song-li-to-lead-who", "date": "2026-10-08", "stream": "news", "headline": "China nominates Song Li to lead WHO", "summary": "China said on Thursday 8 October that it has nominated Song Li, a senior official at its National Health Commission, to succeed Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus as head of the World Health Organization.", "url": "https://www.lemonde.fr/international/article/2026/10/08/pekin-fait-acte-de-candidature-pour-le-poste-de-directeur-general-de-l-oms_6790184_3210.html", "source_domain": "lemonde.fr", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["health", "geopolitics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "China said on Thursday 8 October that it has nominated Song Li, a senior official at its National Health Commission, to succeed Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus as head of the World Health Organization. Tedros's second and final term ends in August 2027. Applications closed on 24 September, but Beijing had not made its candidacy public until now. Foreign ministry spokeswoman Mao Ning presented the bid as support for multilateralism at a time when it \"is under attack\". The WHO Executive Board will shortlist candidates, and the World Health Assembly will choose in May 2027.", "why": "the race decides who leads the Geneva-based agency for the next five years, and Beijing presents its bid as a defence of multilateralism.", "thread_id": "2026-10-08-news-china-nominates-song-li-to-lead-who", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-08", "event_date": "2026-10-08", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["China", "WHO", "Song Li"]}
{"id": "2026-10-08-news-publica-pension-data-leaked-in-cyberattack", "date": "2026-10-08", "stream": "news", "headline": "Publica pension data leaked in cyberattack", "summary": "The federal government confirmed on Thursday 8 October that personal data from Publica, the federal employees' pension fund, leaked after a cyberattack on one of its software suppliers.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/FjG4XOIms04s", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The federal government confirmed on Thursday 8 October that personal data from Publica, the federal employees' pension fund, leaked after a cyberattack on one of its software suppliers. The supplier, PK Softech AG, which builds software for pension funds, detected the attack at the end of September and filed a criminal complaint. The Office of the Attorney General has opened an investigation. According to Publica's letter to its members, which SRF has seen, the leaked data may include names, addresses, AHV numbers (the Swiss social-security number), salaries, pension savings and details of spouses or partners. It is not yet clear whether all of the roughly 66,000 active members and 40,000 pensioners are affected. Publica says the pension money itself is safe, and it is warning members to be careful with unusual calls or messages. It is also unclear whether other pension funds that use PK Softech are affected.", "why": "AHV numbers combined with salary and address data are useful for identity fraud, and the same supplier may serve other Swiss pension funds.", "thread_id": "2026-10-08-news-publica-pension-data-leaked-in-cyberattack", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-08", "event_date": "2026-10-08", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Publica", "PK Softech", "Office of the Attorney General"]}
{"id": "2026-10-08-news-vaud-lays-out-272-million-plan-for-tax-cut", "date": "2026-10-08", "stream": "news", "headline": "Vaud lays out 272-million plan for tax cut", "summary": "Vaud's Council of State proposed on Wednesday 7 October how to cover the CHF 272 million a year in lost tax revenue from the \"12%\" income- and wealth-tax cut that voters approved on 27 September.", "url": "https://www.vd.ch/actualites/communiques-de-presse-de-letat-de-vaud/detail/communique/mise-en-oeuvre-de-linitiative-des-12", "source_domain": "vd.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR"], "topics": ["switzerland", "economy"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Vaud's Council of State proposed on Wednesday 7 October how to cover the CHF 272 million a year in lost tax revenue from the \"12%\" income- and wealth-tax cut that voters approved on 27 September. It proposes CHF 100 million in spending cuts, half on the state's own running costs and half on subsidies, and CHF 172 million in extra revenue. That extra revenue includes CHF 63 million from an additional Swiss National Bank (SNB) payout and CHF 109 million in one-off income. The government wants to phase in the tax cut over several years. It says civil-service salaries will not be cut and that it will still propose indexing pay, and that municipalities are only marginally affected. The measures go to the finance committee as amendments to the 2027 budget, which the Grand Council begins examining on 1 December.", "why": "part of the gap is filled with SNB money and one-off income rather than lasting savings, on top of CHF 260 million already cut in the 2025 and 2026 budgets.", "thread_id": "2026-10-08-news-vaud-lays-out-272-million-plan-for-tax-cut", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-08", "event_date": "2026-10-07", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Vaud", "Council of State", "SNB"]}
{"id": "2026-10-08-news-swiss-wolf-culls-nearly-double", "date": "2026-10-08", "stream": "news", "headline": "Swiss wolf culls nearly double", "summary": "The Federal Office for the Environment (FOEN/OFEV) has approved preventive culls for 39 wolf packs in seven cantons so far this autumn, compared with 22 at the same point last year, Le Temps reported on Thursday 8 October.", "url": "https://www.letemps.ch/articles/la-suisse-autorise-le-tir-de-39-meutes-de-loups-cet-automne-soit-pres-du-double-de-l-an-", "source_domain": "letemps.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "The Federal Office for the Environment (FOEN/OFEV) has approved preventive culls for 39 wolf packs in seven cantons so far this autumn, compared with 22 at the same point last year, Le Temps reported on Thursday 8 October. Graubünden accounts for 20 of the approved requests. A Valais request for the Vallon de Réchy is still being examined, which would bring the total to 40 packs. The culling period runs from 1 September to 31 January. KORA, the foundation that monitors large carnivores for the federal government, told Keystone-ATS that much of the increase comes from a change to the hunting ordinance: FOEN can now authorise culling young wolves before their presence in a pack has been confirmed.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-08-news-swiss-wolf-culls-nearly-double", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-08", "event_date": "2026-10-08", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["FOEN", "Graubünden", "KORA"]}
